<title>USA: Unit Corp Q1 shr $0.16 vs $0.06.</title>
<headline>Unit Corp Q1 shr $0.16 vs $0.06.</headline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p>			    (In thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p> Revenues					$ 24,322	$ 15,871</p>
<p> Income Before Income Taxes		   6,219	   1,952</p>
<p> Net Income					 3,874	   1,219</p>
<p>Net Income Per Common</p>
<p>  Share (Fully Diluted)			  0.16	    0.06</p>
<p>Weighted Average Common</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding (Fully Diluted)     24,531	  21,488</p>
<p>Cash Flow From Operations</p>
<p>  Before Working Capital Changes	   10,552	   5,461</p>
<p> Cash Used in Investing Activities	  8,394	   5,485</p>
<p>SOURCE  Unit Corporation</p>
<p>Revenues from Unit's oil and natural gas operations improved 36 percent in the first quarter to $13.3 million, a result of higher commodity prices and higher natural gas production rates.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
